<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>BurmillaOS</title><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/server/</link><description>Recent content on BurmillaOS</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><copyright>© 2020–2026 [BurmillaOS community](https://github.com/burmilla) · Documentation licensed under [Apache 2.0](https://github.com/burmilla/burmilla.github.io/blob/master/LICENSE)</copyright><atom:link href="https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/server/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title/><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/server/install-to-disk/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/server/install-to-disk/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="installing-to-disk"&gt;Installing to Disk&lt;a class="anchor" href="#installing-to-disk"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;BurmillaOS comes with a simple installer that will install BurmillaOS on a given target disk. To install BurmillaOS on a new disk, you can use the &lt;code&gt;ros install&lt;/code&gt; command. Before installing, you&amp;rsquo;ll need to have already &lt;a href="https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/workstation/boot-from-iso/"&gt;booted BurmillaOS from ISO&lt;/a&gt;. Please be sure to pick the &lt;code&gt;burmillaos.iso&lt;/code&gt; from our release &lt;a href="https://github.com/burmilla/os/releases"&gt;page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="installing-burmillaos"&gt;Installing BurmillaOS&lt;a class="anchor" href="#installing-burmillaos"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;ros install&lt;/code&gt; command orchestrates the installation from the &lt;code&gt;burmilla/os&lt;/code&gt; container. You will need to have already created a cloud-config file and found the target disk.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>iPXE</title><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/server/pxe/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/server/pxe/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="ipxe"&gt;iPXE&lt;a class="anchor" href="#ipxe"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="cp"&gt;#!ipxe&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Boot a persistent BurmillaOS to RAM&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Location of Kernel/Initrd images&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt; base-url &amp;lt;url&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kernel &lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;base&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;-url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;/vmlinuz rancher.state.dev&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;LABEL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;RANCHER_STATE rancher.state.autoformat&lt;span class="o"&gt;=[&lt;/span&gt;/dev/sda&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; rancher.state.wait rancher.cloud_init.datasources&lt;span class="o"&gt;=[&lt;/span&gt;url:http://example.com/cloud-config&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;initrd &lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;base&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;-url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;/initrd&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;boot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you want to autoformat the disk when booting by iPXE, you should add the &lt;code&gt;rancher.state.autoformat&lt;/code&gt; part to kernel cmdline. However, this does not install the bootloader to disk, so you cannot upgrade BurmillaOS.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you don&amp;rsquo;t add &lt;code&gt;rancher.state.autoformat&lt;/code&gt;, BurmillaOS will run completely in memory, you can execute &lt;code&gt;ros install&lt;/code&gt; to install to disk.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>